<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrĕvŏcātus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not called back.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Not asked to repeat a thing; without an encore</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum loca jam recitata revolvimus irrevocati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 1, 223</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That cannot be called</i> or <i>kept
				back</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab acri caede lupus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 11, 401</span></i>
			 (dub.; al. revocatus).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
